-- title:
--   Switcheroo Aggregate Third Term Eq Fourth Term
-- statement:
--   **The third and fourth switcheroo aggregate terms are equal.**
--
--   For every state, indexed polynomial family, and indexed projective submeasurement, the two negative terms in the aggregate qSDD expansion coincide exactly:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{switcherooAggregateThirdTerm}(\mathrm{params},\psi_{bi},\mathrm{family},M)
--   =\operatorname{switcherooAggregateFourthTerm}(\mathrm{params},\psi_{bi},\mathrm{family},M).
--   $$
--
--   This identity removes one independent term from the commutativity switcheroo bookkeeping. The fourth-term chain can therefore be used to analyze both negative contributions in the final aggregate comparison.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooAggregateThirdTerm_eq_fourthTerm`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
